# Path / origin diagrams

When a topic **moves the TCP in space** (OFFSET, INC, frames, square, pallet, pick/place, skip, contour), add a **Path / origin** Mermaid **in addition to** the program-flow chart.

This sketch is **not** millimetres and **not** a cell map. Caption every diagram: study sketch in **UFRAME**; teach on the cell.

GitHub-safe classic syntax only. Do **not** use `@{ shape: }`. Do **not** name a node `io` or `end`.

## When it is required

| Topic | Sketch |
|-------|--------|
| OFFSET | Taught **1-2-3-4**, then same points **1'-2'-3'-4'** after OFFSET CONDITION |
| INC | One taught corner, then **+X / +Y / −X / −Y** deltas (not new named poses) |
| User frame | **World** origin vs **UFRAME** origin on the fixture |
| Square / plot | Corners **1-2-3-4** (FINE stops at each) |
| Pallet | Grid **(row,col)** cells, not twenty copied P[] |
| Pick / place | Home → approach → pick → place → home (heights) |
| Skip | Linear toward dest; leave early at skip fire |
| Circular | Start → **via** → **dest** |

Program flow (L# / diamonds) stays in mermaid-program-flow. **Never** replace a spatial sketch with only a CALL/WAIT flowchart.

## OFFSET (canonical)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  subgraph taught["Taught 1-2-3-4"]
    direction TB
    p1["1"] --> p2["2"]
    p2 --> p3["3"]
    p3 --> p4["4"]
    p4 --> p1
  end
  shift(["OFFSET PR"])
  subgraph off["Same P[] as 1'-2'-3'-4'"]
    direction TB
    q1["1'"] --> q2["2'"]
    q2 --> q3["3'"]
    q3 --> q4["4'"]
    q4 --> q1
  end
  taught ==> shift
  shift ==> off
  classDef proc fill:#DAE8FC,stroke:#6C8EBF
  classDef shiftc fill:#E1D5E7,stroke:#9673A6
  classDef origin fill:#FFF2CC,stroke:#D6B656
  class p1,p2,p3,p4 proc
  class q1,q2,q3,q4 shiftc
  class shift origin
```

## Colors

| Class | Fill | Meaning |
|-------|------|---------|
| `proc` | blue | Taught / first pass |
| `shiftc` | purple | Shifted / primed points |
| `origin` | yellow | Frame origin or OFFSET PR |
| `term` | gray | Home / END pose |

Copy `classDef` from mermaid-program-flow when the same page has a program flowchart.

## NEVER

- Fake plant millimetres as measured fact
- Mix INC arrows onto the OFFSET primed square
- OEM screenshot paste
- One diagram trying to be both L# program flow and a floor sketch

Skill: `fanuc-path-diagram`. Template: `docs/_templates/topic.md` section Path / origin.
